{"topic": "数据结构-AVL", "audience": "", "referenceMaterial": "[none provided]", "allowedTypes": {"chart": "create-chart: Author a chart block for a LectureDoc lecture — a data chart (bar/line/area/scatter) rendered via Observable Plot, theme-aware. Reach for it whenever a page shows numeric comparison, trend over time, share/composition, or correlation — anything where seeing the shape of the numbers beats reading them. Prefer a chart over a table when magnitude/trend/relationship is the point; use a table only for exact nominal lookup where values are not being compared.", "runnable": "create-code-runtime: Author a runnable (edit → Run) code cell block for a LectureDoc lecture — an in-browser Python (Pyodide) + JavaScript editor with a console and a result chart. Reach for it whenever the student should learn by writing/modifying and actually executing code themselves: implementing an algorithm by hand, tuning parameters and seeing the effect, exploratory what-if coding. Use a plain `code` block instead for read-only display the student will not run. Affordances: editable-code, code-execution, console-output, result-visualization. Learner actions: implement, run, debug, modify. Evidence outputs: stdout, execution-result, test-result. Limitations: requires self-contained browser-safe code.", "hero": "create-content: Author static prose and layout blocks for a LectureDoc lecture page — hero, statement, list, agenda, callout, formula, table, code, compare, and grid. Use when a lecture needs narrative or nominal lookup rather than a structural diagram, interactive simulation, quiz, or code runtime. Affordances: prose, fixed-comparison, fixed-sequence, exact-values, read-only-code. Learner actions: read, recall, inspect, compare. Evidence outputs: visible-claim, fixed-steps, exact-lookup, code-example. Limitations: no learner-controlled state, no code execution.", "statement": "create-content: Author static prose and layout blocks for a LectureDoc lecture page — hero, statement, list, agenda, callout, formula, table, code, compare, and grid. Use when a lecture needs narrative or nominal lookup rather than a structural diagram, interactive simulation, quiz, or code runtime. Affordances: prose, fixed-comparison, fixed-sequence, exact-values, read-only-code. Learner actions: read, recall, inspect, compare. Evidence outputs: visible-claim, fixed-steps, exact-lookup, code-example. Limitations: no learner-controlled state, no code execution.", "pullquote": "create-content: Author static prose and layout blocks for a LectureDoc lecture page — hero, statement, list, agenda, callout, formula, table, code, compare, and grid. Use when a lecture needs narrative or nominal lookup rather than a structural diagram, interactive simulation, quiz, or code runtime. Affordances: prose, fixed-comparison, fixed-sequence, exact-values, read-only-code. Learner actions: read, recall, inspect, compare. Evidence outputs: visible-claim, fixed-steps, exact-lookup, code-example. Limitations: no learner-controlled state, no code execution.", "list": "create-content: Author static prose and layout blocks for a LectureDoc lecture page — hero, statement, list, agenda, callout, formula, table, code, compare, and grid. Use when a lecture needs narrative or nominal lookup rather than a structural diagram, interactive simulation, quiz, or code runtime. Affordances: prose, fixed-comparison, fixed-sequence, exact-values, read-only-code. Learner actions: read, recall, inspect, compare. Evidence outputs: visible-claim, fixed-steps, exact-lookup, code-example. Limitations: no learner-controlled state, no code execution.", "agenda": "create-content: Author static prose and layout blocks for a LectureDoc lecture page — hero, statement, list, agenda, callout, formula, table, code, compare, and grid. Use when a lecture needs narrative or nominal lookup rather than a structural diagram, interactive simulation, quiz, or code runtime. Affordances: prose, fixed-comparison, fixed-sequence, exact-values, read-only-code. Learner actions: read, recall, inspect, compare. Evidence outputs: visible-claim, fixed-steps, exact-lookup, code-example. Limitations: no learner-controlled state, no code execution.", "callout": "create-content: Author static prose and layout blocks for a LectureDoc lecture page — hero, statement, list, agenda, callout, formula, table, code, compare, and grid. Use when a lecture needs narrative or nominal lookup rather than a structural diagram, interactive simulation, quiz, or code runtime. Affordances: prose, fixed-comparison, fixed-sequence, exact-values, read-only-code. Learner actions: read, recall, inspect, compare. Evidence outputs: visible-claim, fixed-steps, exact-lookup, code-example. Limitations: no learner-controlled state, no code execution.", "formula": "create-content: Author static prose and layout blocks for a LectureDoc lecture page — hero, statement, list, agenda, callout, formula, table, code, compare, and grid. Use when a lecture needs narrative or nominal lookup rather than a structural diagram, interactive simulation, quiz, or code runtime. Affordances: prose, fixed-comparison, fixed-sequence, exact-values, read-only-code. Learner actions: read, recall, inspect, compare. Evidence outputs: visible-claim, fixed-steps, exact-lookup, code-example. Limitations: no learner-controlled state, no code execution.", "table": "create-content: Author static prose and layout blocks for a LectureDoc lecture page — hero, statement, list, agenda, callout, formula, table, code, compare, and grid. Use when a lecture needs narrative or nominal lookup rather than a structural diagram, interactive simulation, quiz, or code runtime. Affordances: prose, fixed-comparison, fixed-sequence, exact-values, read-only-code. Learner actions: read, recall, inspect, compare. Evidence outputs: visible-claim, fixed-steps, exact-lookup, code-example. Limitations: no learner-controlled state, no code execution.", "code": "create-content: Author static prose and layout blocks for a LectureDoc lecture page — hero, statement, list, agenda, callout, formula, table, code, compare, and grid. Use when a lecture needs narrative or nominal lookup rather than a structural diagram, interactive simulation, quiz, or code runtime. Affordances: prose, fixed-comparison, fixed-sequence, exact-values, read-only-code. Learner actions: read, recall, inspect, compare. Evidence outputs: visible-claim, fixed-steps, exact-lookup, code-example. Limitations: no learner-controlled state, no code execution.", "compare": "create-content: Author static prose and layout blocks for a LectureDoc lecture page — hero, statement, list, agenda, callout, formula, table, code, compare, and grid. Use when a lecture needs narrative or nominal lookup rather than a structural diagram, interactive simulation, quiz, or code runtime. Affordances: prose, fixed-comparison, fixed-sequence, exact-values, read-only-code. Learner actions: read, recall, inspect, compare. Evidence outputs: visible-claim, fixed-steps, exact-lookup, code-example. Limitations: no learner-controlled state, no code execution.", "grid": "create-content: Author static prose and layout blocks for a LectureDoc lecture page — hero, statement, list, agenda, callout, formula, table, code, compare, and grid. Use when a lecture needs narrative or nominal lookup rather than a structural diagram, interactive simulation, quiz, or code runtime. Affordances: prose, fixed-comparison, fixed-sequence, exact-values, read-only-code. Learner actions: read, recall, inspect, compare. Evidence outputs: visible-claim, fixed-steps, exact-lookup, code-example. Limitations: no learner-controlled state, no code execution.", "flow": "create-diagram: Author structural diagram, graph, flow, and timeline blocks for a LectureDoc lecture. Use graph for explicit named edges, branching, hierarchy, or convergence; diagram when a fixed shape carries the relationship; flow for one simple linear chain; timeline only for events with explicit times or stages. Use state-sim when understanding depends on intermediate states or transformations rather than a fixed relationship. Affordances: spatial-structure, node-edge-relations, hierarchy, sequence, chronology. Learner actions: inspect, trace, compare. Evidence outputs: named-relations, fixed-structure, linear-sequence, chronology. Limitations: fixed-state-only, no-coordinate-proof, no-hidden-transition.", "timeline": "create-diagram: Author structural diagram, graph, flow, and timeline blocks for a LectureDoc lecture. Use graph for explicit named edges, branching, hierarchy, or convergence; diagram when a fixed shape carries the relationship; flow for one simple linear chain; timeline only for events with explicit times or stages. Use state-sim when understanding depends on intermediate states or transformations rather than a fixed relationship. Affordances: spatial-structure, node-edge-relations, hierarchy, sequence, chronology. Learner actions: inspect, trace, compare. Evidence outputs: named-relations, fixed-structure, linear-sequence, chronology. Limitations: fixed-state-only, no-coordinate-proof, no-hidden-transition.", "diagram": "create-diagram: Author structural diagram, graph, flow, and timeline blocks for a LectureDoc lecture. Use graph for explicit named edges, branching, hierarchy, or convergence; diagram when a fixed shape carries the relationship; flow for one simple linear chain; timeline only for events with explicit times or stages. Use state-sim when understanding depends on intermediate states or transformations rather than a fixed relationship. Affordances: spatial-structure, node-edge-relations, hierarchy, sequence, chronology. Learner actions: inspect, trace, compare. Evidence outputs: named-relations, fixed-structure, linear-sequence, chronology. Limitations: fixed-state-only, no-coordinate-proof, no-hidden-transition.", "graph": "create-diagram: Author structural diagram, graph, flow, and timeline blocks for a LectureDoc lecture. Use graph for explicit named edges, branching, hierarchy, or convergence; diagram when a fixed shape carries the relationship; flow for one simple linear chain; timeline only for events with explicit times or stages. Use state-sim when understanding depends on intermediate states or transformations rather than a fixed relationship. Affordances: spatial-structure, node-edge-relations, hierarchy, sequence, chronology. Learner actions: inspect, trace, compare. Evidence outputs: named-relations, fixed-structure, linear-sequence, chronology. Limitations: fixed-state-only, no-coordinate-proof, no-hidden-transition.", "freeform": "create-freeform: Author a freeform block for a LectureDoc lecture — the long-tail fallback for a visual relationship that none of the formal block types can express, drawn as inline SVG/HTML restricted to theme colour tokens. Reach for it only after checking the structured types: graph covers trees, DAGs and branching flowcharts; chart covers data; diagram covers fixed shapes; grid and sim.widget cover custom layouts and interactive pieces. When it genuinely is the right tool it now renders as normal page content, so use it without hedging.", "geometry-sim": "create-geometry-sim: Plan a spatial constraint simulation for a LectureDoc lecture. Use when coordinate mapping, dragging, boundaries, vectors, geometric construction, or spatial invariants are themselves the learning evidence. Do not use merely because a state diagram has positioned nodes; AVL rotations remain state-sim. The final block lowers to sim.widget. Affordances: drag, coordinate-map, constraint, construction, spatial-transform. Learner actions: manipulate, construct, predict, inspect. Evidence outputs: coordinate-change, constraint-preservation, spatial-invariant. Limitations: not-decorative-layout, not-discrete-structure, not-code-execution.", "stats": "create-infographic: Author stats blocks for a LectureDoc lecture. Use only to spotlight 2-6 standalone key numbers whose individual magnitude is the evidence; use chart for trends, distributions, or correlations and create-diagram for structural relationships. Affordances: standalone-metrics, fixed-state. Learner actions: inspect, compare. Evidence outputs: key-number. Limitations: no-trends, no-structural-relations, no-unsourced-numbers.", "model-sim": "create-model-sim: Plan a parameterized model simulation for a LectureDoc lecture. Use when learners must change real parameters and observe a recomputed quantitative consequence, compare model regimes, or inspect deterministic or stochastic causal behavior. Use chart for a fixed dataset and state-sim for discrete algorithm steps. Lowers to the shared sim runtime. Affordances: parameter-control, recompute, comparison, stochastic, history. Learner actions: manipulate, predict, calculate, compare. Evidence outputs: parameter-output-map, regime-change, quantitative-cause. Limitations: not-fixed-dataset, not-code-execution, not-discrete-structure.", "quiz": "create-quiz: Author a quiz block for a LectureDoc lecture — objective (multiple-choice, auto-graded) or subjective (open discussion prompt). Reach for it whenever a page should check understanding or provoke reflection rather than only present — at least one per lecture is encouraged. Objective for a checkable fact/skill, subjective for open-ended thinking. Affordances: elicited-response, auto-grading, misconception-diagnosis. Learner actions: predict, calculate, judge, explain. Evidence outputs: student-answer, correctness-feedback, explanation. Limitations: one assessment chain per block.", "state-sim": "create-state-sim: Plan a discrete state simulation for a LectureDoc lecture. Use whenever learning evidence depends on an algorithm's intermediate states, stepwise execution, tree/graph/array mutation, structural transformation, replay, or before-to-after mapping. AVL rotations and data-structure updates belong here even though nodes have positions. The final block lowers to sim.widget. Affordances: state-transition, step, reset, playback, history, comparison. Learner actions: trace, predict, manipulate, construct. Evidence outputs: intermediate-state, transition-sequence, before-after-map. Limitations: not-static-snapshot, not-code-execution, not-coordinate-constraint."}, "currentBrief": {"objective": "学生能说出删除操作与插入操作的主要区别：删除后可能需要多次旋转", "learningAction": "compare", "requiredEvidence": "学生能指出删除后可能需要在多个祖先节点进行旋转", "keyClaim": "AVL 树删除后，从删除点的父节点向上回溯，每个节点都可能失衡，需要多次旋转", "misconception": "删除和插入一样，最多一次旋转就能恢复平衡", "visualTask": "展示一个删除后需要两次旋转的例子", "evidencePolicy": "provided"}, "currentScene": {"id": "delete-overview", "kind": "content", "headline": "删除操作：更复杂的平衡恢复", "lead": "删除节点后，可能需要多次回溯旋转——与插入不同，一次删除可能引发多级不平衡。", "notes": "介绍删除操作的基本思路和与插入的差异", "blocks": [{"type": "sim", "engine": "widget", "html": "<style>
  * { margin: 0; padding: 0; box-sizing: border-box; }
  .root { width:100%; height:100%; min-width:0; min-height:0; display:flex; flex-direction:column; font-family:var(--font-sans, ui-sans-serif,system-ui,sans-serif); background:var(--bg); color:var(--ink); }
  .ctrl-row { display:flex; align-items:center; gap:12px; padding:8px 12px; flex-shrink:0; border-bottom:1px solid var(--line); }
  .ctrl-row button { padding:6px 16px; border:1px solid var(--line); border-radius:6px; background:var(--bg2); color:var(--ink); font-size:13px; cursor:pointer; transition:background .12s, transform .12s; }
  .ctrl-row button:hover { background:var(--accent); color:var(--bg); }
  .ctrl-row button:active { transform:scale(.97); }
  .ctrl-row .step-label { font-size:12px; color:var(--text2); font-variant-numeric:tabular-nums; }
  .stage { flex:1; display:flex; align-items:center; justify-content:center; padding:8px; min-height:0; }
  .stage svg { width:100%; max-width:680px; height:auto; display:block; }
  .readout { display:flex; gap:16px; padding:6px 12px; border-top:1px solid var(--line); flex-shrink:0; font-size:12px; color:var(--text2); }
  .readout span { white-space:nowrap; }
  .readout .hl { color:var(--accent); font-weight:500; }
  .node circle { stroke-width:2; }
  .node text { font-size:13px; text-anchor:middle; dominant-baseline:central; }
  .bf { font-size:11px; text-anchor:middle; dominant-baseline:central; }
  .edge { stroke:var(--line); stroke-width:1.5; fill:none; }
  .deleted { stroke-dasharray:4 3; stroke:var(--text2); }
  .unbalanced .bf { fill:var(--accent); font-weight:600; }
  .balanced .bf { fill:var(--text2); }
</style>
<div class="root">
  <div class="ctrl-row">
    <button id="prevBtn" disabled>← 上一步</button>
    <button id="nextBtn">下一步 →</button>
    <span class="step-label" id="stepLabel">步骤 0 / 3</span>
    <button id="resetBtn">重置</button>
  </div>
  <div class="stage" id="stage"></div>
  <div class="readout" id="readout">
    <span id="statusMsg">初始平衡树</span>
    <span id="rotateMsg"></span>
  </div>
</div>
<script>
  (function(){
    const stepData = [
      {
        label: "初始平衡树",
        nodes: [
          {id:"n50", x:340, y:40, val:50, bf:0, cls:"balanced"},
          {id:"n30", x:200, y:120, val:30, bf:0, cls:"balanced"},
          {id:"n70", x:480, y:120, val:70, bf:1, cls:"balanced"},
          {id:"n20", x:100, y:200, val:20, bf:0, cls:"balanced"},
          {id:"n40", x:300, y:200, val:40, bf:0, cls:"balanced"},
          {id:"n60", x:420, y:200, val:60, bf:0, cls:"balanced"},
          {id:"n80", x:560, y:200, val:80, bf:0, cls:"balanced"},
          {id:"n10", x:40, y:280, val:10, bf:0, cls:"balanced", deleted:false},
          {id:"n25", x:160, y:280, val:25, bf:0, cls:"balanced", deleted:false}
        ],
        edges: [
          ["n50","n30"],["n50","n70"],
          ["n30","n20"],["n30","n40"],
          ["n70","n60"],["n70","n80"],
          ["n20","n10"],["n20","n25"]
        ],
        status:"初始平衡树",
        rotate:""
      },
      {
        label: "删除节点 10",
        nodes: [
          {id:"n50", x:340, y:40, val:50, bf:1, cls:"balanced"},
          {id:"n30", x:200, y:120, val:30, bf:1, cls:"balanced"},
          {id:"n70", x:480, y:120, val:70, bf:1, cls:"balanced"},
          {id:"n20", x:100, y:200, val:20, bf:-1, cls:"unbalanced"},
          {id:"n40", x:300, y:200, val:40, bf:0, cls:"balanced"},
          {id:"n60", x:420, y:200, val:60, bf:0, cls:"balanced"},
          {id:"n80", x:560, y:200, val:80, bf:0, cls:"balanced"},
          {id:"n10", x:40, y:280, val:10, bf:0, cls:"balanced", deleted:true},
          {id:"n25", x:160, y:280, val:25, bf:0, cls:"balanced", deleted:false}
        ],
        edges: [
          ["n50","n30"],["n50","n70"],
          ["n30","n20"],["n30","n40"],
          ["n70","n60"],["n70","n80"],
          ["n20","n10"],["n20","n25"]
        ],
        status:"删除节点 10 后，节点 20 失衡 (BF=-1)",
        rotate:"需要旋转"
      },
      {
        label: "第一次旋转 (右旋 20)",
        nodes: [
          {id:"n50", x:340, y:40, val:50, bf:1, cls:"balanced"},
          {id:"n30", x:200, y:120, val:30, bf:1, cls:"balanced"},
          {id:"n70", x:480, y:120, val:70, bf:1, cls:"balanced"},
          {id:"n25", x:100, y:200, val:25, bf:0, cls:"balanced"},
          {id:"n40", x:300, y:200, val:40, bf:0, cls:"balanced"},
          {id:"n60", x:420, y:200, val:60, bf:0, cls:"balanced"},
          {id:"n80", x:560, y:200, val:80, bf:0, cls:"balanced"},
          {id:"n20", x:40, y:280, val:20, bf:0, cls:"balanced", deleted:false}
        ],
        edges: [
          ["n50","n30"],["n50","n70"],
          ["n30","n25"],["n30","n40"],
          ["n70","n60"],["n70","n80"],
          ["n25","n20"]
        ],
        status:"右旋节点 20 后，节点 30 失衡 (BF=2)",
        rotate:"节点 30 仍失衡，需要第二次旋转"
      },
      {
        label: "第二次旋转 (左旋 30)",
        nodes: [
          {id:"n50", x:340, y:40, val:50, bf:0, cls:"balanced"},
          {id:"n40", x:200, y:120, val:40, bf:0, cls:"balanced"},
          {id:"n70", x:480, y:120, val:70, bf:0, cls:"balanced"},
          {id:"n25", x:100, y:200, val:25, bf:0, cls:"balanced"},
          {id:"n30", x:300, y:200, val:30, bf:0, cls:"balanced"},
          {id:"n60", x:420, y:200, val:60, bf:0, cls:"balanced"},
          {id:"n80", x:560, y:200, val:80, bf:0, cls:"balanced"},
          {id:"n20", x:40, y:280, val:20, bf:0, cls:"balanced", deleted:false}
        ],
        edges: [
          ["n50","n40"],["n50","n70"],
          ["n40","n25"],["n40","n30"],
          ["n70","n60"],["n70","n80"],
          ["n25","n20"]
        ],
        status:"左旋节点 30 后，整树恢复平衡",
        rotate:"全部平衡"
      }
    ];

    let step = 0;
    const stage = document.getElementById('stage');
    const stepLabel = document.getElementById('stepLabel');
    const statusMsg = document.getElementById('statusMsg');
    const rotateMsg = document.getElementById('rotateMsg');
    const prevBtn = document.getElementById('prevBtn');
    const nextBtn = document.getElementById('nextBtn');
    const resetBtn = document.getElementById('resetBtn');

    function render(s) {
      const d = stepData[s];
      const W = 680, H = 360;
      let svg = `<svg viewBox="0 0 ${W} ${H}" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg">`;
      // edges
      d.edges.forEach(e => {
        const p1 = d.nodes.find(n => n.id===e[0]);
        const p2 = d.nodes.find(n => n.id===e[1]);
        if(p1 && p2) {
          svg += `<line class="edge" x1="${p1.x}" y1="${p1.y}" x2="${p2.x}" y2="${p2.y}"/>`;
        }
      });
      // nodes
      d.nodes.forEach(n => {
        const cls = n.deleted ? 'deleted' : '';
        const fill = n.deleted ? 'var(--bg2)' : 'var(--bg)';
        const stroke = n.deleted ? 'var(--text2)' : 'var(--accent)';
        const bfCls = n.cls === 'unbalanced' ? 'unbalanced' : 'balanced';
        svg += `<g class="node ${bfCls}">`;
        svg += `<circle cx="${n.x}" cy="${n.y}" r="22" fill="${fill}" stroke="${stroke}" class="${cls}"/>`;
        svg += `<text x="${n.x}" y="${n.y}" fill="var(--ink)">${n.val}</text>`;
        svg += `<text class="bf" x="${n.x+30}" y="${n.y-8}" fill="var(--text2)">BF=${n.bf}</text>`;
        svg += `</g>`;
      });
      svg += '</svg>';
      stage.innerHTML = svg;
      stepLabel.textContent = `步骤 ${s} / 3`;
      statusMsg.textContent = d.status;
      rotateMsg.textContent = d.rotate;
      prevBtn.disabled = (s === 0);
      nextBtn.disabled = (s === 3);
    }

    function update() {
      render(step);
    }

    prevBtn.addEventListener('click', function(){
      if(step > 0) { step--; update(); }
    });
    nextBtn.addEventListener('click', function(){
      if(step < 3) { step++; update(); }
    });
    resetBtn.addEventListener('click', function(){
      step = 0; update();
    });

    // initial paint
    render(0);

    // verification
    console.assert(stepData.length === 4, "应有4个步骤");
    stepData.forEach((d,i) => {
      console.assert(d.nodes.length > 0, `步骤${i}应有节点`);
      console.assert(d.edges.length > 0, `步骤${i}应有边`);
    });
  })();
